.he "unlz4 (1)                    9/28/26                    unlz4 (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
unlz4
- decompress the LZ4 frame format
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
unlz4 [ infile [ outfile ] ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Unlz4 reads an LZ4 frame and writes the original bytes.  With no
argument, or where a name is -, it reads the standard input and writes
the standard output.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
A frame carrying a content size or block or content checksums is
accepted, and those fields are skipped; the header checksum is read but
not verified.  The history window is 16383 bytes, matching lz4, so a
larger offset is rejected.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
lz4 (1), tar (1)
